This seems like further circumvention of the problem to me.
It would be better to have a better check for if the work should be canceled or not. because in this case it doesn't need to be canceled, which is why it returns EALREADY.
The work->work_q is not reset to NULL once finished, so it shouldn't be used in all this error handling.

The check above for example:
```
	if (work->work_q != NULL && work->work_q != work_q) {
		err = -EADDRINUSE;
		goto done;
	}
```
Is this one the correct behavior?
